      "id": "uc-002",
      "name_en": "Internal Document Summarisation",
      "name_ar": "تلخيص الوثائق الداخلية",
      "description_en": "An AI system used by trained government staff to summarise internal ministry documents, reports, and correspondence. The audience is domain-expert civil servants, not the general public.",
      "description_ar": "نظام ذكاء اصطناعي يستخدمه موظفو الحكومة المدرَّبون لتلخيص الوثائق والتقارير والمراسلات الداخلية للوزارات. والجمهور المستهدف موظفون مدنيون متخصصون لا عامة الجمهور.",
      "use_case_class": "document_summarisation",
      "confidence_threshold": 0.90,
      "weighting_rationale": "Internal document summarisation serves trained government staff who have domain expertise to catch errors and who operate within established administrative oversight structures. The primary risk is an inaccurate summary that propagates a decision error through the bureaucratic process. Accuracy controls therefore dominate the mandatory weight. Privacy controls are the second-ranked group because government documents routinely contain personal data about citizens (case files, correspondence, HR records) and the summarisation process must not create privacy risks through inappropriate aggregation or leakage. Security controls are mandatory because documents may contain commercially sensitive or classified information susceptible to prompt injection via document content. The lower confidence threshold of 0.90 reflects that staff users have professional judgment to validate outputs and that human oversight is the operating norm rather than an exception in this context.",
